meridian oss
============

build:  make
run:    make run          (rebuilds meridian.db from data/)
check:  make check        (billing rule checks, bin/billing-test)
reg:    make register     (invoice register for 2026-07)
demo:   make demo         (invoice-api :8082 + dashboard pages on :8083)

binaries land in bin/

  mediation      nightly ingest, writes meridian.db
  inventory-api  :8081   /sites  /circuits  /capacity
  billing-run    monthly invoice register, --json for the reconciliation feed
  billing-test   billing rule checks
  invoice-api    :8082   /invoices?acct=...&period=...  (bearer token, audited)
  ipam           management address report (10.20.0.0/16)

dashboard/index.html and dashboard/billing.html are static pages, open them in
a browser with inventory-api and invoice-api running.

invoice-api returns customer names, tax ids, service addresses and balances,
so every request needs "Authorization: Bearer <token>". callers and the
accounts each one may see are listed in billing/invoice-api/clients.conf
(gitignored, chmod 600, format in clients.example; --clients to override).
the server will not start without at least one caller. every request, allowed
or denied, is appended to invoice-api-audit.log (--audit-log to override) with
time, peer, caller, filters and the ACCT_ID/PERIOD pairs returned. make demo
writes a random demo key to clients.conf if there is none; paste the token
into the API key box on dashboard/billing.html.

dashboard/capacity.html is the sales desk capacity check. it asks
/capacity?requested=<mbps> and shows what is left at each customer location.
available = total - allocated, we do not hold back a maintenance buffer.
serviceable locations come from data/locations.csv.

data/ holds the telemetry drops. billing/accounts/ is the account master.

billing rules, one file each, all of them go through billing/invoice.cpp:

  rating.cpp      whole gigabytes, partial gigs round up, $10 a gig over plan
  proration.cpp   30 day billing month, mid cycle plan changes split on it
  promo.cpp       promo credits expire at the end of the cycle they were issued
  suspension.cpp  a suspended line is billed the full month, no credit
  lines.cpp       3-9 lines 5% off recurring, 10+ lines 10%
  latefee.cpp     10 day grace after the due date, then 1.5% of the balance
  tax.cpp         GST/HST on the pre discount amount, PST/QST on what is paid
  discounts.cpp   loyalty credit off the subtotal

the provinces we bill are BC, AB, ON and QC. the province is on the account
record (PROVINCE=) and on the invoice register page.

vantage-telco rates the same accounts differently. tools/parity in that repo
runs both registers off the same usage feed and prints the differences.

contacts: ops-eng (pager), billing questions -> finance
